-I know, I know it's not, but in the back of my head,

00:57:06.600 --> 00:57:08.400
I'm like, "Then I'll start doing that again."

00:57:08.400 --> 00:57:11.740
-No, that's a very bad idea for so many reasons.

00:57:11.740 --> 00:57:13.340
-I think people will be happy to see me.

00:57:13.340 --> 00:57:14.840
-Sure. -Do you think it's the --

00:57:14.840 --> 00:57:16.360
-Oh, look! Are you --

00:57:16.360 --> 00:57:19.910
I think you're getting invited for tonight.

00:57:19.910 --> 00:57:21.110
-I think tonight. -Yeah.

00:57:21.110 --> 00:57:22.210
-Okay, but here's the thing.

00:57:22.210 --> 00:57:25.250
Can we move it from midnight to, like, 6:00?

00:57:25.250 --> 00:57:30.000
Uh, we saw a clip from your fantastic new show, "Sunny."

00:57:30.030 --> 00:57:31.530
This is a lot of different things.

00:57:31.530 --> 00:57:33.870
-It's a lot of things. -This is a show about technology.

00:57:33.870 --> 00:57:36.690
This is a show about grief. This is a mystery.

00:57:36.690 --> 00:57:38.190
It must have been such a cool thing

00:57:38.190 --> 00:57:40.030
when it first came across your desk.

00:57:40.030 --> 00:57:42.730
-It was, yeah. It's very -- it's very odd.

00:57:42.730 --> 00:57:44.530
But I think in, like, the best way,

00:57:44.530 --> 00:57:46.530
it felt wholly original to me.

00:57:46.530 --> 00:57:49.360
And I haven't really had the chance to be that person

00:57:49.360 --> 00:57:51.060
who's, like, the middle of a mystery

00:57:51.060 --> 00:57:53.760
where you're just, like, sustaining tension

00:57:53.760 --> 00:57:55.660
and worried about who's chasing you

00:57:55.660 --> 00:57:57.360
and who you're chasing the entire show.

00:57:57.360 --> 00:57:58.760
So that was, like, kind of a new challenge for me.

00:57:58.760 --> 00:58:00.000
And it was shot in Japan.

00:58:00.120 --> 00:58:01.920
-Yes, and you were -- we were texting,

00:58:01.920 --> 00:58:04.460
and you told me you were in Japan for a while.

00:58:04.460 --> 00:58:05.860
-Six months, yeah. -Six months.

00:58:05.860 --> 00:58:09.560
And what was your -- how was your cultural integration to Japan?

00:58:09.560 --> 00:58:12.560
-Fantastic. You know, I had been there before.

00:58:12.560 --> 00:58:15.370
I love Japan. I'm -- everything in Japan, you're like,

00:58:15.370 --> 00:58:18.690
"Oh, this is, like, the most amazing ramen I've ever had.

00:58:18.690 --> 00:58:20.990
Like, this is the best shopping experience of my life.

00:58:20.990 --> 00:58:23.490
Look at the way they're packing those pencils."

00:58:23.490 --> 00:58:25.790
Like, the first week I was on the show,

00:58:25.790 --> 00:58:28.690
I was, like, just in the haze of my love,

00:58:28.690 --> 00:58:30.000
the romanticism of Japan.

00:58:30.060 --> 00:58:32.320
and we worked late, and I had a burger,

00:58:32.320 --> 00:58:35.360
and I was like, "This is the best burger I've ever had.

00:58:35.360 --> 00:58:37.660
Japan does everything so well. Where is this from?"

00:58:37.660 --> 00:58:39.160
And they were like, "Burger King."

00:58:39.160 --> 00:58:40.700
It was from Burger King.

00:58:40.700 --> 00:58:43.080
But better. It was better there.

00:58:43.080 --> 00:58:46.990
-Sunny is sort of a personal assistant,

00:58:46.990 --> 00:58:48.300
and you did an interview recently.

00:58:48.300 --> 00:58:49.800
This is an Apple show, and you were saying

00:58:49.800 --> 00:58:52.500
that you don't look at your Apple -- your iPhone

00:58:52.500 --> 00:58:54.850
the same way anymore after working with Sunny.

00:58:54.850 --> 00:58:56.650
-She's more than a personal assistant.

00:58:56.650 --> 00:58:58.750
She's like a grief assistant. -That's true, yes.

00:58:58.750 --> 00:59:00.000
-That's true, yes. -You know, she's, like,

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:03.000
But, yes, there is something about having this, like,

00:59:03.000 --> 00:59:05.820
little physical round white thing

00:59:05.820 --> 00:59:09.820
that feels like an exaggerated version of your iPhone

00:59:09.820 --> 00:59:11.820
with expressions and emotions.

00:59:11.820 --> 00:59:14.820
And it's at least -- I don't know. At least she has feelings.

00:59:14.820 --> 00:59:16.960
I mean, she probably doesn't really have feelings,

00:59:16.960 --> 00:59:17.960
but she looks like she has feelings,

00:59:17.960 --> 00:59:20.960
whereas your phone's just like, "You need an update."

00:59:20.960 --> 00:59:21.960
That's --

00:59:21.960 --> 00:59:24.970
-You reunited with Sonny for the press tour.

00:59:24.970 --> 00:59:25.970
Was it nice to see her again?

00:59:25.970 --> 00:59:28.970
-Isn't she cute? Yes. It really was.

00:59:28.970 --> 00:59:30.000
- It really was, I didn't realize

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:31.640
I missed her?"

00:59:31.640 --> 00:59:33.440
I'm like, "You're not real, but I did.

00:59:33.440 --> 00:59:36.130
I missed her." I was like, "Sonny, you!"

00:59:36.130 --> 00:59:38.830
-How was acting with your robot companion?

00:59:38.830 --> 00:59:41.130
-It was interesting. It was super interesting.

00:59:41.130 --> 00:59:44.530
Joanna Sotomayor plays her voice and does her expression.

00:59:44.530 --> 00:59:45.830
So, like -- -She's there.

00:59:45.830 --> 00:59:49.170
-She's there. No, she's in a tent near the set,

00:59:49.170 --> 00:59:51.870
and she had, like, a camera on a helmet,

00:59:51.870 --> 00:59:55.320
and it would translate her expressions to Sonny's face.

00:59:55.320 --> 00:59:56.920
-Oh, my God. -Simultaneously.

00:59:56.920 --> 00:59:58.920
-So, were there times where she was rolling her eyes

00:59:58.920 --> 01:00:00.000
at your acting?

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:02.990
-Yeah, that. -A lot of size.

01:00:02.990 --> 01:00:05.770
-Like, get it together, lady. Yeah.

01:00:05.770 --> 01:00:08.570
-That's very cool. You've had to do this before.

01:00:08.570 --> 01:00:10.270
You did it with one of the all-time greats, though,

01:00:10.270 --> 01:00:14.630
where it's not an actual, you know, fellow human.

01:00:14.630 --> 01:00:17.030
-Yes. -You worked with Kermit.

01:00:17.030 --> 01:00:18.750
I got to work with Kermit. -The GOAT.

01:00:18.750 --> 01:00:22.990
-I mean, look at that. The best.

01:00:22.990 --> 01:00:25.830
-This was the 2011 Muppets movie.

01:00:25.830 --> 01:00:28.140
When you went into your work with Kermit,

01:00:28.140 --> 01:00:30.000
what was your level of excitement?

01:00:30.120 --> 01:00:35.160
insane off the charts my first day on this movie all of the Muppets were in my

01:00:35.160 --> 01:00:39.220
office and I was telling them that they were no longer relevant which was the

01:00:39.220 --> 01:00:43.720
best acting I've ever done because nobody's more relevant but isn't it

01:00:43.720 --> 01:00:47.320
weird like you talk to him and then you just talk to him well it was funny I did

01:00:47.320 --> 01:00:51.060
a weekend update once with Kermit and the funny thing is they tell you which

01:00:51.060 --> 01:00:54.130
I'm sure they told you as well like just remember to look at Kermit don't

01:00:54.130 --> 01:00:56.880
look at yeah don't look at the person doing the voice yeah and you're like all

01:00:56.880 --> 01:01:00.000
right that'll be tricky and then the minute Kermit starts talking you're like I'm not taking

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:01.900
I've never taken my eyes off you maybe ever.

01:01:01.900 --> 01:01:02.900
-Ever.

01:01:02.900 --> 01:01:04.660
Even when the cameras weren't rolling,

01:01:04.660 --> 01:01:08.960
we were having, like, small talk, banter.

01:01:08.960 --> 01:01:11.960
-Yeah. And then I'm also like, "Hey, I don't know how to tell you.

01:01:11.960 --> 01:01:15.320
There's a dude underneath you.

01:01:15.320 --> 01:01:19.840
If that's a problem, blink twice."

01:01:19.840 --> 01:01:21.940
-I got you. -I don't like that there's this dude down there.

01:01:21.940 --> 01:01:23.840
-We can get out of here right now.

01:01:23.840 --> 01:01:27.280
-I feel like he's eavesdropping on us.

01:01:27.280 --> 01:01:30.000
And so, at the end of the day,

01:01:30.280 --> 01:01:33.660
It must be so exciting, too, because this does feel like --

01:01:33.660 --> 01:01:34.940
you know, "page turn" is the wrong word,

01:01:34.940 --> 01:01:37.200
but, like, it's so exciting to know what's gonna happen next.

01:01:37.200 --> 01:01:38.800
And when you were reading the scripts for "Sunny,"

01:01:38.800 --> 01:01:40.260
was that the feeling you had, as well?

01:01:40.260 --> 01:01:41.740
-Yes. I binged.

01:01:41.740 --> 01:01:45.140
I did whatever the reading version of "Binges."

01:01:45.140 --> 01:01:46.940
Where I really wanted to know what happened

01:01:46.940 --> 01:01:47.840
when we got to the end.

01:01:47.840 --> 01:01:50.340
And that's -- I feel like that is the feeling of the show,

01:01:50.340 --> 01:01:52.240
is you're like, "Oh, no. What's next?"

01:01:52.240 --> 01:01:54.040
-It was, like, nothing I've seen before.

01:01:54.040 --> 01:01:55.240
I'm so excited to watch more.

01:01:55.240 --> 01:01:56.900
And it's just a delight to have you here.

01:01:56.900 --> 01:01:58.640
-Always a delight to be here. -Welcome back to New York City.

01:01:58.640 --> 01:01:59.760
We miss you. -Thank you. Thank you.

